music BGM08D.mp3
sound C.aac
text As always, I finish up work and get into the passenger's seat of Yoshino-san's truck.
text I look at the landscape flowing by, at the salarymen and at the students returning home, and stare into space, thinking about my value in society.
text As always, Yoshino-san is silent.
text Making up for that, the radio has been running, covering up the vacuum of our silence.
text That was our usual routine.
if intF[613] == 0
	goto s16
fi
goto 18
label s16
text An intense guitar intro comes forth from the speakers.
text Then come the drums, along with a shout.
text It's a voice I remember hearing somewhere.
text I wonder where...
text As I think about it, Yoshino-san turns the radio tuner.After some noise, the radio switches to live coverage of a professional baseball game.
text That's also where I let my thinking come to a halt.
sound ~
if rtf1 != ""
	jump $rtf1 $rtl1
fi
jump $rtf0 $rtl0
label 18
text From the speakers comes forth an intro I remember hearing before.
text It's an intense guitar rhythm, as if the artist is just hacking away at the strings.
text Then come the drums, along with a shout.
text Aah, that's a coincidence if I ever saw one...
text I look at Yoshino-san's profile.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
sound QDW.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text ...That's right. You lied to me long ago, didn't you?
text @[Tomoya]
text Huh?
sound QDX.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text You said you played the drums.
text @[Tomoya]
text O-Oh, yeah...
sound QDY.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text And the other guy'd also never played a guitar before in his life, wasn't that right?
text @[Tomoya]
text That's right...
sound QDZ.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text What was that all about?
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
choice Answer honestly|Try and deceive him somehow
