label 22
text @[Tomoya]
text Um, I can actually sing the entire song from memory.
text @[Yoshino]
text ...
text I sing along to the melody coming from the radio.
text I really sing it, with no mistakes at all.
text Although I did say I could sing it, I was surprised I actually managed it.
text What started it all was me destroying Sunohara's mixtape...
text but after that, I got so interested in him that I even bought his CD myself.
text I think back on when I listened to it every day for a period of time.
text @[Tomoya]
text (I really listened to it a lot, huh...)
text The radio has already gone on to the next song.
text It's a hip-hip song that sounds like it might be popular.
text One that Sunohara might have liked.
text @[Tomoya]
text To be honest, I'd forgotten about it until now...
text @[Tomoya]
text But I kind of feel like listening to it again now.
text @[Tomoya]
text Though I don't actually have that many CDs, and I don't normally listen to music all that much, either...
text @[Tomoya]
text So I bought it, despite that.
text @[Yoshino]
text ...
sound ~
text Yoshino-san stops the vehicle.
text We're back at the station.
sound QE3.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text ...Shall I tell you an old story?
text @[Tomoya]
text Huh?
sound QE4.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text It's a story about a certain young rocker.
text @[Tomoya]
text Ah, okay.
text I answer like that without thinking, but...
text I wonder if this really a story I am supposed to hear.
text I guess I ended up proving it to him.
text Just how much I like his song.
text This is my own responsibility.
text A responsibility I should have born last year to begin with.
sound QE5.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Let's go grab some coffee first, then.
