sound QGK.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text One day, he was approached with a proposal for a TV program.
sound QGL.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text It was to be a documentary about him going around visiting his fans.
sound QGM.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text They weren't just normal fans, either.
sound QGN.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text They were those who were saved by his music... and were still facing adversity even then.
sound QGO.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Until then, he'd continued to obstinately refuse any request to be on television. However...
sound QGP.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text ...he could sense the director's sincere attitude about the whole thing...
sound QGQ.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text ...and more than anything, he figured it would be best for his future if he interacted with his fans.
sound QGR.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text And thus, filming started.
sound QGS.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He'd gotten an idea of what it would be like from letters...
sound QGT.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text ...but the scene in front of his eyes was just overwhelming.
sound QGU.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text It was even greater than he had imagined.
sound QGV.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He met people who had crumbled ─ both their lives and their actual bodies...
sound QGW.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text ...people who were truly using his songs as a crutch, and he felt he was being relied upon.
sound QGX.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text At that time, he realized.
sound QGY.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text That his words... no longer belonged to just him.
sound QGZ.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text However...
sound QH0.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He truly didn't understand at all.
sound QH1.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He didn't understand why it was that his songs provided salvation in their hearts in the first place.
sound QH2.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text After that, they would still be looking to him as a crutch.
sound QH3.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Just how was he supposed to respond to that...?
sound QH4.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text The music he had composed up until then had always been solely for himself.
sound QH5.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text A place where he wouldn't be reproved for doing what he himself wanted. That was all the music world had been for him.
sound QH6.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He had no memory of ever having sung for someone else.
sound QH7.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text But because of that project, he could no longer remain unaware of it.
sound QH8.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Those with physical handicaps...
sound QH9.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Those who live while suffering tremendously because of their parents.
sound QHA.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Those whose minds were weak, and seemed even now like they were about to break down...
sound QHB.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text And those were just a small part of them...
sound QHC.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text There were thousands, tens of thousands, that he hadn't even met who were also looking to his music for aid...
sound QHD.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text And he was made to realize... that he had to start making music for their sake now.
sound QHE.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text When filming ended, he was asked to sing one of his songs with an acoustic guitar for the ending of the show.
sound QHF.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text But his hands were shaking at that point, and he couldn't play properly.
sound QHG.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text They had to change the program's ending to a scene of him walking, with his CD playing in the background.
sound QHH.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text And then...
sound QHI.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text After filming ended, he became unable to compose music anymore.
sound QHJ.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He couldn't even sing the songs he'd been singing up until then with a straight face.
sound QHK.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Now that he knew the truth, he could only ridicule himself for the shallow songs he had written up until then.
sound QHL.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Reality is something far, far more overwhelming.
sound QHM.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text All he knew was superficial nonsense. At best, he had just been trying to act cool.
