sound QHV.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text ...committed a crime.
sound QHW.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text A big crime. One that cannot ever be undone.
music BGM29.mp3
sound QHX.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text A face he recognized... was displayed on TV.
sound QHY.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He thought it was all his fault.
sound QHZ.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text It was all because he let himself come to a stop.
sound QI0.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text ...He simply had to go on.
sound QI1.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He had to keep on going, for the sake of those that needed him.
sound QI2.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Thinking that, he grabbed his guitar...
sound QI3.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text ...and started singing again.
sound QI4.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text It was probably from there... that he started running himself to ruin.
sound QI5.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He became unable to distinguish what he was singing from reality.
sound QI6.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text It had reached the point that he started living a life of ideals.
sound QI7.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Fixated on the idea that that was what everyone needed...
sound QI8.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Even he didn't really understand why he was singing these things.
sound QI9.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text But he shook off his doubts... and continued singing.
sound QIA.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text It was a battle.
sound QIB.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text But as he continued fighting, he continued making enemies.
sound QIC.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He continued bellowing; he continued verbally assaulting them.
sound QID.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Toward the enemies he himself was continuing to create...
sound QIE.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text In the end, his ideals and lip service simply didn't stand a chance to them anymore.
sound QIF.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text In order to mow them down, he had no other choice but to strike out at reality itself.
sound QIG.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Because there was nothing more pitiful than the reality he was facing at that moment.
sound QIH.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text As a result, his songs deviated from ideals, and instead became something degenerate.
sound QII.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text They no longer granted hope or courage, just the bitterness of reality.
sound QIJ.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He even stopped singing his love songs.
sound QIK.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text They were unsightly.
sound QIL.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Whenever he was about to sing, he'd get sick to his stomach.
sound QIM.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text All of it was hypocrisy.
sound QIN.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He was projecting a false image.
sound QIO.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He couldn't even understand himself anymore.
sound QIP.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text His lyrics became inconsistent.
sound QIQ.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Once he got to his second line, he'd already contradicted his first.
sound QIR.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He even sang that if you want to live, then you should die.
sound QIS.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text It was just abnormal.
sound QIT.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text All that was left... was for his pretenses to come falling down.
sound QIU.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He was supposed to just sing whatever he wanted to sing.
sound QIV.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text It had been hopeless to try to sing just to save other people.
sound QIW.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text It could only end with him breaking down.
sound QIX.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Maybe he shouldn't have been so weak.
sound QIY.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text No, that's wrong. If he was too strong, that itself would have been hypocrisy.
sound QIZ.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He felt sick to his stomach...
sound QJ0.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He was in constant contradiction with himself.
sound QJ1.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text But he also had to cover up those contradictions somehow.
sound QJ2.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text In the midst of his contradictions, he had to pretend as if he hadn't noticed them.
sound QJ3.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Because he was scared of losing his music.
sound QJ4.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Music was the only thing he had.
sound QJ5.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text And to protect that, he turned to drugs.
sound QJ6.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He was already in complete contradiction now.
sound QJ7.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text The music he had depended on so people wouldn't hold him in contempt...
sound QJ8.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text In order to protect that, he started doing something so incredibly contemptable...
sound QJ9.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text But at the time, he didn't even realize that.
sound QJA.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Because he'd succeeded at masking all of his contradictions to the public.
sound QJB.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text As long as he continued doing drugs, he continued wanting to sing.
sound QJC.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Even if he couldn't sing properly, he would still record his songs.
sound QJD.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He'd buy his drugs himself, late at night.
sound QJE.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Carefree from any suspicions.
sound QJF.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text But he got tracked soon enough.
sound QJG.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He was tried for his crime, and locked up in prison.
music ~
sound QJH.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Before he knew it, he was lying on top of a white hospital bed, being treated for drug dependence.
sound QJI.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He had his mind and body completely rinsed...
sound QJJ.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text And when he finally left the hospital...
sound QJK.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He'd lost his place in the world.
music BGM18B.mp3
sound QJL.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Just about everyone knew his face.
sound QJM.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text As an insane rocker that failed in trying to found a cult.
sound QJN.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Everyone was pointing at him, whispering behind his back.
sound QJO.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text It was the destruction of someone who had made a mistake.
sound QJP.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Just where was he supposed to go to now?
sound QJQ.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text With that tainted body of his.
sound QJR.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Even if he washed his body, his sin would be stuck on him for the rest of his life.
sound QJS.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Along with his face that everyone knew.
sound QJT.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He'd lost music, he didn't have any parents... there was nothing left for him to do.
sound QJU.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text As is the nature of good-for-nothing people like him...
sound QJV.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text ...after losing his sole support in life...
sound QJW.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text ...all that was left was to keep on falling down, without restraint.
sound QJX.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He started living like a vagrant.
sound QJY.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He even continued perpetuating his crimes.
sound QJZ.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text It was his only choice.
sound QK0.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He started thinking that if living itself was really such an ugly thing, then he'd rather lose his life.
sound QK1.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He spent every day in the depths of the abyss.
sound QK2.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text And amidst a life like that, this is what he wished, just once...
sound QK3.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text "I want to go back to my hometown..."
sound QK4.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text If he could go back to that time he enjoyed most in life, even if for just a second...
sound QK5.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text That's all he wanted...
sound QK6.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text So, solely for that reason...
sound QK7.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text He returned to his old home where he was born and raised.
setvar strS[1000] = "BG033"
