text @[Nagisa]
text I met Ibuki-sensei today.
text @[Tomoya]
text Oh, yeah, you went there today.
text @[Tomoya]
text So, what happened?
sound QMM.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text Yes. I told her my impressions.
sound QMN.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text And she was really surprised when I did.
text @[Tomoya]
text You're not telling me even Ibuki-sensei didn't know Yoshino-san was a former musician, are you...?
sound QMO.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text No, no, of course she knew that.
sound QMP.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text I'm sure she was just surprised that I was so moved by this... rock music, is what it's called?
sound QMQ.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text And then she told me this.
sound QMR.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text "I really wish Yoshino-san would go back to his music."
text @[Tomoya]
text I'm pretty sure he still sings for Ibuki-sensei, though... or am I wrong?
sound QMS.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text Yes, that's right.
sound QMT.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text But Ibuki-sensei said she wanted far, far more people to hear him sing...
sound QMU.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text Because Yoshino-san's music is beautiful and passionate...
sound QMV.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text I agree with her.
text @[Tomoya]
text I see now...
text @[Tomoya]
text So even his actual girlfriend, Ibuki-sensei, agrees...
text @[Tomoya]
text I bet she's probably always wanted to do something about it...
text But it's exactly because she knew of his past, that she must have not been able to make the suggestion.
text So when faced with the reality that Nagisa, a girl that doesn't seem like she'd be interested in rock at all, was so moved by it, she must have re-evaluated the situation.
text Thinking that Yoshino-san really should continue moving people's hearts.
text @[Tomoya]
text Say, Nagisa.
sound QMW.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text Yes?
text @[Tomoya]
text How about you help, too?
